                "Take the boat from Stormwind Harbor to Auberdine;",
                "",
                "",
                "",
            },
        },
        trash = {
            { title = "Living grass (Pokémon mechanic)",
              text = "The most dangerous section is the grass around Saltspine: Thicket Lurkers are not stealthed — walking through tall grass spawns them, Pokémon-style. Thicket Matriarchs are spread around the area and screech for Lurker reinforcements at low health. Stay out of the grass, take the narrow path, fight in open areas, and when fighting Matriarchs kill the non-Matriarch mobs first so the screech summons as few extras as possible." },
            { title = "Themed packs",
              text = "The creatures inside are raptors (Thicket Lurker, Thicket Hunter, Thicket Matriarch), crocolisks, Highland spiders, a bog beast (Highland Creeper) and turtles — their names match the four areas." },
        },
        bosses = {
            { en = "Saltspine",
              text = "A very simple fight as long as you clear out the nearby mobs first. Saltspine casts Thunder Clap on the tank — a heavy slow that does not change how you play — and periodically Dust Storm on everyone within 10 yards, reducing attacks' chance to hit by 25%; casters should stay out of melee range." },
            { en = "Shadetooth",
              text = "Shadetooth is joined by two Thicket Hunters; fighting all three at once is very difficult unless overleveled — either CC the adds for the whole fight, or CC one and kill the other first. Dispel the Hunters' poison quickly. Once only the boss remains: Tendon Rip hits the tank moderately, and Terrifying Roar is a 5-second undispellable fear — easy to get feared into grass-spawned raptors or uncleared adds. Clear the crocodile cove to the left and fight there; the Hunters cannot swim, so dragging the boss back into the previous boss area resets it. The boss can be slowed and stunned, which is especially useful during Frenzy below 30%." },
            { en = "Highland Horror",
              text = "It is the target of the Alliance quest \"Horrors in the Highland\" — kill it inside the dungeon and bring the root core back to Rethiel the Greenwarden." },
            { en = "Relic Guardian",
              text = "The encounter starts by pressing the Archival Panel on the right side of the inactive boss. This is a gear and level check: the difficulty comes from high tank damage and a large health pool. The boss casts Thunder Clap on everyone within 10 yards — a heavy movement/attack-speed slow plus moderate damage. The tank is periodically knocked back and sometimes stunned for 5 seconds. The boss can be stunned and slowed: use CC liberally and kite between the nearby structures." },
        },
    },
    city_of_dalaran = {
        tagline = "The rebuilt dome-less city of Dalaran: sneak into this magical capital through its sewers and face rogue arcane constructs and rampant fel energy — 8 bosses (1 of them hidden).",
        tips = {
            "The entrance is not on the streets: drop through a grate into the sewers, cross the Underbelly and follow a long pipe to a purple portal. The Horde-side gate is opened with a Dalaran Sewer Key.",
            "Nearly every mob in the dungeon is immune to Arcane damage: Arcane damage spells (Arcane Missiles, Arcane Explosion, etc.) and interrupts cast as Arcane (like Counterspell) all fail here — mind your damage composition when forming the group. Constructs and elementals are also immune to Bleed and Poison, and treants are immune to Nature damage.",
            "Mana Phantoms (non-elite) cast Mana Burn, which is very taxing on whoever is targeted — interrupt or focus them. The Saturated Remnant leaves behind a mana-restoring field on death; make use of it.",
            "Unstable Sentinel's Malfunction has a 2-second wind-up, then hits everyone within 25 yards repeatedly for 6 seconds: ranged stay beyond 25 yards for the whole fight, melee run out when you see the wind-up.",
            "The Shade of the Archmage is the final boss: when his mana runs out he Mass Polymorphs the whole party, then channels Awakening to refill it; Bounding Mana is a targeted arcane boomerang that silences for 6 seconds anyone it passes through — don't stand in line with the target; you can hide behind walls to avoid Mass Polymorph, but pulling him out of the room fully resets him.",
            "Rough order of progress: clear Atrexis the Grave Knight in the sewers first; the hidden boss Lyn the Ignored also lives in the sewers (you must forge the Dalaran Codex via the Shadowfang Keep and Ambermill steps before you can summon her); after the sewers, Arcane Anomaly, Arcanic Enigma and Unstable Sentinel roam the streets, and Mana Devourer guards the Violet Hold entrance; the Fel Ancient is locked behind the mana barrier in mid-city; the Shade of the Archmage waits at the end.",
            "Wipe recovery is painful: the Spirit Healer sits at the graveyards in Hillsbrad Foothills (separate Alliance/Horde ones), so the ghost run back to the dungeon is long — try to secure a combat rez instead of releasing.",
            "Forever adds a Kirin Tor reputation; the Kirin Tabard asks for exalted: most enemies give 5 points, sewer elites 12-13, Atrexis 15, and Lyn the Ignored and the Shade of the Archmage 25 each.",
        },
        entrance = {
            H = "Dalaran sits in the Alterac Mountains; the city-gate pin is at about 8.0, 61.2 on the Alterac map. Fastest Horde route: run from Undercity through Silverpine Forest, swim across from the Silverpine coast and land at The Sepulcher in the Ruins of Lordaeron, then walk a few minutes. Inside the city, take the special tunnel — the Image of Archmage Modera grants Horde access; opening the gate requires at least one player with a Dalaran Sewer Key.",
            A = {
                "Take the boat from Stormwind Harbor to Auberdine;",
                "Switch boats on the other side of the Auberdine dock to Menethil Harbor;",
                "Stay on this boat until it takes you to Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills;",
                "Follow the road north from Southshore into the Alterac Mountains (a bit of a hike the first time) and find the rebuilt, dome-free city of Dalaran;",
                "Inside the city, drop through a street grate into the sewers and cross the Underbelly;",
                "Follow the long pipe to its end and enter the purple portal.",
            },
        },
        trash = {
            { title = "Arcane Immunity",
              text = "Almost every mob in this dungeon is immune to Arcane damage — keep that in mind if you normally use spells like Arcane Missiles or Arcane Explosion to deal damage, or Counterspell to interrupt." },
            { title = "Mana Phantoms",
              text = "Non-elite mobs that cast a very nasty Mana Burn which should be interrupted. They should be focused down quickly." },
            { title = "Saturated Remnant",
              text = "Once defeated it leaves behind an area that restores mana to whoever stands inside it — make sure to make use of that field." },
            { title = "Kirin Tor Necromancers",
              text = "In the Underbelly, necromancers stand around a ritual circle heaped with bodies and skeletons keep rising from it. Kill the necromancers first or the skeletons will stack up on you." },
            { title = "Angry Tomes",
              text = "Enchanted books around the Magus Commerce Exchange that spawn from the buildings as you approach the Unstable Sentinel. Clear them before the pull or keep them controlled — they add up fast." },
            { title = "Mana Barrier",
              text = "The Fel Ancient in mid-city is guarded by a mana barrier and a grove of Suffused Treants — clear the treants first, then talk to Magus Fansy Goodbringer south of the barrier to remove it; only then is the boss unlocked." },
            { title = "Street patrols",
              text = "Kirin Tor mages and arcane golems are dense along the streets — hug walls, watch the patrols; a Mana Wraith occasionally springs out of the trash packs." },
        },
        bosses = {
            { en = "Atrexis the Grave Knight",
              text = "Atrexis the Grave Knight stands by a ritual circle early in the sewers, surrounded by Kirin Tor necromancers — a very easy tank-and-spank. His primary mechanic is summoning Skeletons — non-elite mobs that keep climbing out of the circle; kill them on sight. The fight has no time-sensitive mechanics, and the only way to die is popping heavy AOE before the tank has established threat. He periodically disarms the active tank for about 6 seconds — use defensives while disarmed; his hard-hitting abilities on the tank are nothing to sneeze at, so bring a shield for this one." },
            { en = "Lyn the Ignored",
              text = "Lyn the Ignored is a hidden boss deep in the sewers and must be summoned first: 1) kill Archmage Arugal in Shadowfang Keep and take the Black Tome from the book on his room's table; 2) in the keep at Ambermill, Silverpine Forest, use the tome next to the blue crystal Leyline Focus to turn it into the Dalaran Codex; 3) back in the sewers, after Atrexis don't take the right-hand path up to the streets — go straight into the room with the purple rune circle and have the Codex carrier click it — Lyn steps out from the round iron grate gate (with a wink to Ragnaros). The fight itself is surprisingly punishing: she periodically hurls Shadow Bolts for noticeable damage; Bramble Curse is a 1.5-second cast, 3-minute curse that makes the afflicted hurt themselves when attacking — brutal for melee, dispel it; she also raises two non-elite skeletons — kill them promptly." },
            { en = "Arcane Anomaly",
              text = "Arcane Anomaly guards the city right after the sewers, with a signature mechanic that will kill you if mishandled: Focused Blast fires a beam in front of it after a 3-second cast, lasting 6 seconds and hitting four times a second, sweeping the whole room counterclockwise — raid veterans will recognize the C'thun / Halion / Norushen beam; touching it is lethal, so leave the beam's path as soon as the cast starts. Between beams it hits the tank with a 1.5-second Arcane Bolt. Engaging also spawns small adds at the edge of the room — keep the group inside the circle on the platform to avoid dragging them into the boss." },
            { en = "Arcanic Enigma",
              text = "Arcanic Enigma waits on the eastern side of the city streets. Two Mana Phantoms accompany the boss — their Mana Burn is very taxing on whoever is targeted, so burn them down quickly (no extra Phantoms spawn, but the boss continuously summons small Arcane Manalings — cleave and AOE them down, lower priority than the Phantoms). Mana Morph turns a player into an animal for 8 seconds — it is a Magic effect, have someone dispel it; the boss also hits nearby targets with AOE Arcane damage and silence — healers keep their distance at all times." },
            { en = "Unstable Sentinel",
              text = "Unstable Sentinel stands around the Mage District. Its one defining mechanic, Malfunction: after a 2-second cast it hits everyone within 25 yards for roughly 140 Arcane damage every 2 seconds for 6 seconds — ranged stay beyond 25 yards for the whole fight, melee run out on the wind-up; with enough level and gear melee can tank through it, but being kind to your healer is the baseline. Note: non-elite Angry Tomes spawn from the buildings as you approach — clear them before engaging." },
            { en = "Mana Devourer",
              text = "Mana Devourer resides by the entrance to the Violet Hold — deceptively difficult: it periodically deals damage to everyone within 45 yards and drains 200 mana; it also casts Siphon Vitality on the active tank — a Magic debuff dealing about 65 Arcane damage every 2 seconds for 10 seconds, dispel it. The fight is essentially a race against time — the group's mana will run out sooner or later, so the faster you kill it the better; the boss is immune to Arcane. Clear all the trash in the boss area first — it will join the fight otherwise." },
            { en = "Fel Ancient",
              text = "The Fel Ancient is protected by a mana barrier in mid-city, watched over by Suffused Treants: clear the treants first, then talk to Magus Fansy Goodbringer south of the barrier to remove it before engaging. Two mechanics stacked together are deadly: Entangle occasionally roots 2 targets and deals damage over time; Fel Timbers charges a player, hitting everyone within 5 yards and leaving a damaging fel pool on the ground — while rooted, be sure to dodge the timber and the pool; movement removers like a paladin's Hand of Freedom or Escape Artist are worth a lot here." },
            { en = "Shade of the Archmage",
              text = "The Shade of the Archmage is the final boss, waiting in the Violet Chamber — the Image of Archmage Modera opens a portal to bring the group to him. He powers his abilities with his mana pool, and once it drains he Mass Polymorphs the whole party for 8 seconds, then channels Awakening for 6 seconds to refill it. His primary damage on the tank (Arcane Explosion) is high and steady; he also periodically deals moderate damage to everyone within 20 yards. Occasionally he casts Bounding Mana — an orb flies to a random player and back to him, dealing Arcane damage and a 6-second silence to anyone it passes through: spread out, don't stand between him and the target, and keep casters at max range. Casters looking to squeeze out extra damage or healing can hide behind the wall during Mass Polymorph — but careful: if anyone leaves the room during the fight, he fully resets. The Legacy challenge counts the dungeon as done when he dies." },
        },
    },
